      rule: "<p><b>A successful Title VII plaintiff can recover (slide 29):</b></p><ul><li>Back pay and reasonable attorneys' fees</li><li>Equitable relief, including reinstatement and seniority</li><li>Punitive damages for <b>intentional</b> discrimination</li></ul><p>The sum of compensatory and punitive damages is <b>capped</b> by the size of the employer.</p><p><b>Defenses to a Title VII action (slide 30):</b></p><ul><li><b>Merit:</b> work history, qualifications, and so on</li><li>A <b>seniority system</b> that rewards long-term employees</li><li><b>Bona fide occupational qualification (BFOQ)</b></li><li>Discrimination for a reason <b>other than race or color</b> is permitted if it's <b>job related</b> and a <b>business necessity</b></li></ul><p><b>BFOQ examples (slide 31):</b> gender-specific clothing (for example, modeling it), religious establishments, airline pilots, law enforcement, firefighters, and actors.</p>",
